    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90562.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "This is now a choice election between the future and the past. Trump is the past. He's a creature of the 70s and the 80s from real estate development and reality TV shows. Biden and Trump were wildly unpopular. A lot of voters didn't want them. Now Harris arrives. She will pick a running mate. And this is the next generation. Now does Harris have weaknesses? Yeah. But this turns Trump into the old man from the 70s and 80s. And Harris is a 59-year-old prosecutor from California, a creature of the new generation. So it's now a choice selection between the future and the past. And that always favors the future. Whether Harris can prosecute the case is a big question. She's got weaknesses. But as we'll see with our guest, they can be overcome. I talk about this with a former Republican congressman named Bob Nay. You may not know Bob Nay, but he was a Republican from Ohio. He came into Congress with the sort of the Newt Gingrich crowd and the contract with America. Bob now is a radio journalist who serves a lot of radio shows around the country. and gives reports on politics to those radio shows. He's really interesting because he sees everything from both sides. He's that Midwest kind of ex-congressments. So he understands JD Vance, he understands the Trump thing, and he also understands where the Democrats are going and where he thinks they should go. So with that, let's just jump right in with our conversation with Bob Nae. Bob, thank you for joining. The reason I wanted to have you on is because, you know, as a former congressman from the Republican side, I mean, we're hearing all from all the Democratic bigwigs. But what I'm interested in is hearing about what's going on inside the minds of sort of Republican Trump land now that Biden has dropped out. I suppose we should recap and say Biden's dropped out, you know, from my own kids to everybody in the Democratic establishment, there's new energy. It's a whole new race. Sure. The Trump people come out of a pretty successful convention. But now they're facing somebody that they, I don't think, expected to face. What's your first reaction to the whole Biden withdrawal?",
