    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "I don't think Kevin that they ever thought Biden would actually get out. I think they thought he would remain. And I did last week at one point in time. Then when I saw Pelosi and Schumer, I've served with both of them. Hakeem Jeffries, I haven't. But when I saw some of the statements, you know, I can read congressional speak in between the lines, I thought, okay, this is not going good. Then Schumer visited personally with the president, and I kind of knew that was it. You know, once you have that going on, it's a problem. So at 146 on Sunday, he drops out. He turns around, I think within an hour or so, and he endorses Kamala Harris. And by four o'clock, she's in the race. Then all of the money has been legally turned over. It went from Biden for president to Harris for president. She's got all the money. Now, Barack Obama came out and said, Open Convention, the Clintons immediately said, okay, Kamala, you're ours. I joked, I wonder what they asked for before they did that, you know, they did it. And Obama really did the right move. Obama was pretty smart about it. Let's have an open convention. Now, there's a difference between open and contested because, as you know, Kevin, if nobody steps up to the plate, I'd say in the next few days, besides Joe Manchin, Uh, who is the former Democratic senator from West Virginia across the river from me unless somebody steps up. It's an uncontested convention and I do want to add this because of a weird thing that happened in the state of Ohio. four years ago and we've covered this on your show your home state right my home state well four years ago Trump and Biden didn't make the ballot in Ohio 90 days before you got to be certified as the candidate through your convention they didn't make the ballot so high legislature republic can control four years ago said sure we'll waiver you well this time Trump made the ballot to the convention was early Biden didn't and a Republican Republican legislature said well we'll think about it Our governor, Mike DeWine, did the right thing and came out and said, okay, men and women, stop it, do this. Now, meanwhile, the Democrats rightfully didn't trust the Ohio Republican-controlled legislature, so they had this virtual roll call planned. Ohio corrected the problem, but guess what's still out there? The virtual roll call. So they're probably, probably going to institute that even though they don't have to, to certify if it's Kamala Harris before the convention starts. I really wanted to mention that because then I don't care about super delegates or thousands of delegates. If she's certified by roll call, she's certified.",
