  },
  {
    "episode_id": 90562,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90562.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "Well, that's a really interesting question because you have the world of two trumps. And Corey Lewandowski said it best, yeah, let Trump be Trump. Because Trump was having a great big argument in the campaign when Corey was still running it, people were going to Corey, you've got to do this, you've got to tell him that, and he said let Trump be Trump. Now, things have changed. I don't care how ego-driven, egocentric, narcissistic, you know who I'm talking about, that you are, which Trump can be put into those categories. You have a situation where within half a centimeter you would be dead, half an inch, I should say. It has to do something to somebody. I'm not talking about total transformation, but there has to be some human situation there where it changes you a little bit. Even with this guy? Yes, you said it best. Even with this guy. We saw it, I think, at the convention. I'm going, if I'm running the Trump campaign, they're going to have to convince Trump because Trump's going to go out there. He's going to do that come by law. You know, now we did before. But he's got to be careful because I don't think you want to feed into the misogynistic and any form of, you know, racist attitude. I think that it's better to tie her legitimately to immigration. Absolutely. So I heard that. But I think tying her as the liberal with Biden, and she's nothing but Biden, number two, she even took all his money. I think that's the route to go.",
