    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "I mean, I watched Buttigieg's last election. And the Wisconsin station I do, the guy that has his program up there, he's basically, you know, a Republican and think, but he loved Buttigieg. And Buttigieg's performed well, I thought. I really did. I thought he performed well. I had talked to, as I do, both sides of the aisle. I've got friends, Democratic consultants, Republicans. And I had talked to, excuse me, a Republican or a Democratic consultant who brought up the issue. And I don't reveal his name because I promised him I wouldn't at the time. He brought up the issue. He said, I don't think we've got the guts to put a gay man at the front of the ticket. And he told me that. I said, well, that kind of sounds surprising. I mean, out of a Democrat consultant, he said, Bob, I want to win elections, which was fascinating. But I think for Kamala Harris, I don't think it would be a bad move. I really don't. A bad move at all. Buttigists can handle himself quite well. uh, you know, he'd be going against JD Vance and the debates and Buttigieg in my opinion is a good debater. So that would be one. Now, if, um, I was putting together my dream ticket, uh, if I was a Democrat campaign consultant, I would want Kelly Whitmer is what I would the governor of Michigan, Whitmer. I think she would be a great addition to the ticket in Kelly. He's from Arizona. democrat his wife was shot gabby giffords when she was a congresswoman i think that would be a pretty pretty good ticket",
